  "description": "WUMXAD crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group P n -3 n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C160 H152 Dy9 O42 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(C1 H4 O1),C1 H1 Cl3. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1K (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1I (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1KA (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1J (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1LA (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1JA (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1UA (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.604-5.097 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.36-167.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C169H177Cl3NO44Dy9. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
